# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Node — build-time only, never runs in production (D7)
node_modules/
dist/
.angular/

# Local data. The database is also the public audit log, so a stray copy is not harmless.
#
# Both suffixes, because the two that matter disagree: the README and `--db`'s default say
# `vriltrainer.db`, the systemd unit says `.db`, and only `.sqlite` was listed here — which is how
# six dev databases reached a public repository. A committed database is worse than clutter: it
# invites someone to trust a chain head that no deployment ever wrote.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Secrets and environment
#
# `token.key` is the one secret this product has (D9). It seals the trial tokens, so a leaked copy
# lets anyone mint a token claiming any target — which is the single thing that would make the
# published proof worthless. Everything else in the database is public on purpose; this is not, and
# the README tells people to create it right here in the repository root.
.env
.env.*
token.key
*.key

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log

# Pre-existing entry, kept
deleteme.md
src/app/verify/derivation.vectors.json
client/dist/
